## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/segmentbyconnectivity.html
- Summary (EN): Segment by Connectivity splits a layer into connected regions according to a connectivity rule you choose. It outputs an integer ID per region and a mono alpha mask.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Segment by Connectivity découpe une couche en régions connexes selon une règle de connexité, chaque région recevant un identifiant entier.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the layer in which connectivity is detected (the only input)"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: the layer type the source accepts", "Connectivity: Below Threshold, Above Threshold, At Threshold (neighbours on the same side of the threshold connect), At Levels (pixels in the same value band connect; band width equals Threshold)", "Threshold: connectivity threshold, or band width with At Levels; an eyedropper can set it", "Offset: with At Levels, shifts where the bands split", "Collapse IDs: remaps IDs to range from zero to the number of segments", "Outputs: id (unique integer per region, -1 for non-matching regions) and alpha (mono, 1 where the rule is met)"]

- Caveats: ["The id output can change when the resolution changes, since island shapes change the ID order", "Collapse IDs makes results more stable but not fully consistent; the ordering depends on each region's first pixel, so do not rely on it for animated sources", "Without Collapse IDs, the IDs are effectively random when the resolution changes"]

